   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved social protection to all workers with special focus on informal workers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sri Lanka is strengthening its social protection system to deliver broader coverage, adequate benefits, and coordinated support for informal, domestic, and migrant workers, thereby reducing vulnerability to poverty and economic shocks. Through ILO support, inclusive and financially sustainable social protection schemes are being advanced to improve income security and access to essential services across the life cycle. These reforms are contributing to a more coherent, resilient, and equitable social protection system, benefiting vulnerable workers, migrant workers, and the ageing population, and are implemented through a coordinated, tripartite partnership involving government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
